.DS_Store
tests/e2e/artifacts/
junit.xml

# Accounts database - local state, and it would be a credential leak in a
# public repo (scrypt hashes, but still every registered address).
data/*.db

# Deployment secrets. NEVER commit a real SECRET_KEY or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build / CI artifacts
junit_e2e.xml
screenshots/
*.PNG
!app/static/**/*.png
# The pixel gate's baselines. `*.PNG` is meant for the screenshots that pile up
# in the project root, but git's ignore matching is case-insensitive on Windows,
# so it was also swallowing all 49 of these: they existed on one machine and
# were tracked NOWHERE. A baseline that is not versioned cannot gate anything —
# a fresh clone has none, `golden.py --pixels` then writes whatever the code
# currently renders, and the gate passes by having nothing to compare against.
# That is this repo's signature failure: a check that looks green and is inert.
!tests/golden/pixels/*.png
